6. Choosing the structure
Choose the most appropriate structure and explain why:

ordered student registrations
fast username membership checking
employee_id → employee
immutable (x, y) coordinates
frequent insertion/removal from both ends
Choose from:

list / tuple / set / dict / deque
Need	Structure	Why
ordered student registrations	list	keeps insertion order, can keep growing
fast username membership checking	set	O(1) lookup via hashing, instead of scanning
employee_id → employee	dict	direct key → value lookup, not position-based
immutable (x, y) coordinates	tuple	locked, can't be accidentally changed
frequent insertion/removal from both ends	deque	O(1) at both front and back, list is only cheap at the back
One-line rule for each:

Need order, might grow → list
Need fast "does it exist" → set
Need label → value → dict
Need "never change" → tuple
Need fast work at both ends → deque

